# Docs Auto-Sync (read-only drift audit)

## What this skill does

Compares the **code** in `spring-ai-alibaba-admin` against the two doc files
that humans read to understand the system, and prints a structured drift
report:

- `docs/api-list.md` ←→ `*Controller.java`
- `docs/data-model.md` ←→ `*DO.java` / `*Entity.java` / `docker/middleware/init/mysql/*-schema.sql`

The output is a markdown report **only**. The skill exits with a "0 files
modified" line so the user knows nothing was changed behind their back.

## What this skill explicitly does NOT do

Hard contract — violating any of these means the skill is broken, not
"helpful":

- ❌ No `Write`, no `StrReplace`, no `Shell`. The `allowed-tools` list
  enforces this at the tool layer.
- ❌ Never propose a `git commit`, never suggest running `mvn` / `make`,
  never trigger downstream skills (`scaffold-resource`, etc.).
- ❌ Never auto-apply a "fix" even when the fix is obviously one-line
  trivial.
- ✅ Allowed: include the exact text snippet the user could paste, clearly
  fenced and labelled `suggested patch (paste manually)`.

If the user, after seeing the report, asks "go ahead and fix it", **stop
this skill** and switch to a write-capable skill (e.g. `scaffold-resource`
for new tables, or plain edits). Do not silently extend this skill's scope.

## Inputs to gather

Ask in **one** consolidated round; if the user gave no input at all,
proceed with the defaults below.

| Parameter | Required? | Default | Notes |
|-----------|-----------|---------|-------|
| `scope` | no | `both` | `api` / `data` / `both` |
| `since` | no | (full scan) | git ref like `HEAD~10` or a date; narrows the audit to recently-touched files only — purely advisory, the skill itself does not call git |
| `domain` | no | `both` | `admin` / `studio` / `both` (filter to one persistence convention) |
| `severity_floor` | no | `info` | `info` / `warn` / `error` — hide items below this level |

Don't ask follow-ups for missing optional inputs. Just print which defaults
you applied at the top of the report.

## Sources of truth

Live code (authoritative):

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| Admin REST endpoints | `spring-ai-alibaba-admin-server-start/src/main/java/com/alibaba/cloud/ai/studio/admin/controller/*Controller.java` |
| Studio REST endpoints | `spring-ai-alibaba-admin-server-start/src/main/java/com/alibaba/cloud/ai/studio/admin/builder/controller/*Controller.java` |
| Admin entities | `spring-ai-alibaba-admin-server-start/src/main/java/com/alibaba/cloud/ai/studio/admin/entity/*DO.java` |
| Studio entities | `spring-ai-alibaba-admin-server-core/src/main/java/com/alibaba/cloud/ai/studio/core/base/entity/*Entity.java` |
| Admin DDL | `docker/middleware/init/mysql/admin-schema.sql` |
| Studio DDL | `docker/middleware/init/mysql/agentscope-schema.sql` |

Doc files (audit targets):

- `docs/api-list.md` — endpoint list grouped by resource
- `docs/data-model.md` — table list grouped by domain (§2 admin, §3 studio,
  §4.1 entities without a single matching table)

## Workflow

Run steps strictly in order. After each step print the count of items found
so the user can follow progress.

| # | Step | Tool | Concrete action |
|---|------|------|-----------------|
| 1 | Confirm inputs | (chat) | Print resolved `scope` / `domain` / `since` / `severity_floor` once. Do not ask follow-ups for optional fields. |
| 2 | Enumerate code endpoints | `Glob` + `Read` | Glob the two controller dirs. For each `*Controller.java`, extract: class-level `@RequestMapping` prefix, method-level `@GetMapping/@PostMapping/@PutMapping/@DeleteMapping/@RequestMapping` value, HTTP verb, method name, return type. Store as `(verb, full_path, controller_class, method_name)`. |
| 3 | Enumerate doc endpoints | `Read` + `Grep` | Read `docs/api-list.md`. Parse every endpoint row (markdown table rows starting with HTTP verb or with `\| <verb> \| <path>` shape, plus any inline `### <verb> <path>` headings). Store as `(verb, full_path, section_title, line_no)`. |
| 4 | Diff endpoints | (in-memory) | Produce three lists: (a) **MISSING_IN_DOC** — in code, not in doc; (b) **MISSING_IN_CODE** — in doc, not in code (dead doc); (c) **MISMATCH** — same `(verb, path)` but conflicting parameter / response shape. For (c) only flag the easy-to-detect cases: differing HTTP verb on same path, differing path-variable names, request-body class renamed. Do NOT try to deep-diff field-level request bodies — too noisy. |
| 5 | Enumerate code tables | `Glob` + `Read` | Read both `*-schema.sql` files; parse every `CREATE TABLE` block into `(table_name, [(column, sql_type, nullable, default, comment)])`. Read every `*DO.java` / `*Entity.java`; parse fields via Lombok / JPA / MyBatis-Plus annotations into `(java_field, java_type, column_name_if_annotated)`. |
| 6 | Enumerate doc tables | `Read` | Parse `docs/data-model.md` section by section. Pick up `### x.y <table_name>（<cn name>）` subsection headers and the immediately-following `字段 \| SQL 类型 \| 说明` table rows. Store as `(table_name, [(column, sql_type, description)])`. |
| 7 | Diff data model | (in-memory) | Produce four lists: (a) **TABLE_MISSING_IN_DOC** — in DDL, not documented; (b) **TABLE_MISSING_IN_DDL** — documented but no `CREATE TABLE` (cross-reference §4.1 "no single table" entries — those are not bugs, only flag truly orphaned tables); (c) **FIELD_MISSING_IN_DOC** — column in DDL but not in doc table; (d) **FIELD_TYPE_MISMATCH** — column present in both but `sql_type` string differs (case-insensitive, with `BIGINT(20)` == `BIGINT` normalization). |
| 8 | Cross-check Entity ↔ DDL | (in-memory) | For each table, line up DDL columns against entity fields. Flag: column in DDL not mapped on entity, entity field with `@Column`/`@TableField` pointing to a non-existent column. Skip the conventional bookkeeping columns (`id`, `gmt_create`, `gmt_modified`, `create_time`, `update_time`, `workspace_id`, `deleted`, `status`) unless they themselves disagree. |
| 9 | Assemble report | (in-memory) | Render the report in the format below. Apply `severity_floor` filter last. |
| 10 | Print report | (chat) | Output the report verbatim. End with the explicit `Files modified: 0` line and the next-step menu. |
| 11 | Stop | (chat) | Do not propose `git commit`, do not chain into other skills. Wait for the user to decide. |

## Diff classification rules

Severity scale:

| Severity | Meaning | Examples |
|----------|---------|----------|
| `error` | Doc is misleading — a reader following the doc will get wrong behaviour. | endpoint in doc returns `Result<Foo>` but code returns `PageResult<Foo>`; doc lists a column type `VARCHAR(64)` that DDL says `TEXT`. |
| `warn` | Doc is incomplete — reader gets less than the truth. | new endpoint in code not listed in doc; new column in DDL not listed in doc. |
| `info` | Doc is verbose / stale but harmless. | doc lists an endpoint whose path has since moved; doc still mentions a deprecated DO. |

Auto-downgrade rules (avoid spam):

- A controller method annotated `@Deprecated` → endpoint diffs against it are `info`, not `warn`.
- A doc subsection inside `## 4.1 API 中存在但无对应单表的实体声明` → flagged
  `TABLE_MISSING_IN_DDL` items here are downgraded to `info` (these are
  in-memory / external by design).

## Report format

Single markdown report, sections in this fixed order:

```markdown
# Docs Drift Report

_Generated by `docs-auto-sync` (read-only). Files modified: 0._

**Scope**: api+data | **Domain**: admin+studio | **Since**: full scan | **Floor**: warn

## Summary

| Category | error | warn | info | total |
|----------|------:|-----:|-----:|------:|
| API: missing in doc        | 0 | 3 | 0 | 3 |
| API: missing in code       | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |
| API: signature mismatch    | 2 | 0 | 0 | 2 |
| Data: table missing in doc | 0 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| Data: field mismatch       | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
| Entity ↔ DDL mismatch      | 0 | 2 | 0 | 2 |
| **Total**                  | **3** | **7** | **2** | **12** |

## 1. API endpoints

### 1.1 Missing in docs/api-list.md (warn)

- **`POST /api/dataset/version/diff`** — `DatasetController.diffVersion`, line 187
  - suggested patch (paste manually, into §2 "数据集" of docs/api-list.md):
    ```markdown
    | POST | /api/dataset/version/diff | 比较两个数据集版本差异 |
    ```

### 1.2 Documented endpoints with no matching controller method (info / warn)

- **`GET /api/legacy/foo`** — appears in docs/api-list.md L92, no matching method.
  - Likely deleted in commit XXXXXXX (user can verify); remove the doc row.

### 1.3 Signature mismatch (error)

- **`GET /api/experiment/{id}`** — doc says returns `Result<Experiment>`, code returns `Result<ExperimentDetail>` (`ExperimentController.java:62`).

## 2. Data model

### 2.1 Tables in DDL but not in docs/data-model.md (warn)

- **`workflow_run`** — defined in `admin-schema.sql:412`, missing from §2.
  - suggested patch (paste manually, into §2):
    ````markdown
    ### 2.7 workflow_run（工作流运行实例）
    | 字段 | SQL 类型 | 说明 |
    |------|----------|------|
    | id | BIGINT(20) UNSIGNED | 主键 |
    | ... | ... | ... |
    ````

### 2.2 Field type mismatch (error)

- Table `dataset_item`, column `content`:
  - DDL: `LONGTEXT NOT NULL`
  - doc/data-model.md L143: `TEXT`
  - Recommendation: update doc to `LONGTEXT NOT NULL`.

### 2.3 Entity ↔ DDL mismatch (warn)

- `DatasetItemDO.tags` (java) ↔ DDL has no `tags` column on `dataset_item`.
  - Either add a `tags` column + migration, or drop the field from the DO.

## 3. Next steps for the human

This skill made **0 file modifications**. Pick one:

1. Apply the patches above by hand.
2. Ask another skill (or a fresh chat) to apply them — explicitly say
   "apply the docs-auto-sync report" so the agent has authorization.
3. Ignore. If an item is intentional drift, add a one-line note in the
   relevant doc so the next run downgrades it to `info`.
```

The actual numbers and entries above are illustrative — fill in real
findings, omit empty sections, keep ordering stable so diffs across runs
are reviewable.

## Pitfalls to avoid

- **Don't deep-diff request body shapes** at field granularity — it is too
  noisy and the doc rarely tracks DTO refactors. Flag only the four
  signature-mismatch cases listed in step 4(c).
- **Don't normalise column types aggressively.** `DATETIME` vs `TIMESTAMP`
  is a real difference; `BIGINT(20)` vs `BIGINT` is cosmetic. The
  normalisation list in step 7(d) is intentionally short — extend only
  when the user complains about false positives.
- **Don't confuse the two domains.** Admin DOs live in `server-start/admin/entity`;
  studio entities live in `server-core/.../core/base/entity`. Same class
  simple name can exist in both domains and refer to different tables.
- **Don't follow links into related skills.** If a finding looks like
  `scaffold-resource` would fix it, mention the skill name in the report
  but do not invoke it.
- **Don't print a finding without a line number / file path.** The whole
  point of this report is "go look here". A finding without a location is
  noise.
- **Don't suppress an empty section silently if `severity_floor` filtered
  everything out.** Render it as `(no items at or above the current floor)`
  so the user knows the audit ran.

## When to re-run

- After merging any PR that touches a `*Controller.java`,
  `*DO.java` / `*Entity.java`, or `docker/middleware/init/mysql/*.sql`.
- Before opening a PR that itself modifies `docs/api-list.md` or
  `docs/data-model.md` — to make sure you are documenting reality and not
  inventing it.
- As a weekly hygiene check; the report is cheap (read-only), so cost of
  running it is near zero.
